{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"cb8d90f6cb8d854b","name":"card_event_provence_landing","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_provence_landing","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PROVENCE LANDING","text":"Units you deploy this turn move into the frontline if possible.","flavorText":"On August 15, 1944, the Allied forces launched Operation Dragoon, the landing in Provence. A fleet of nearly 2,000 ships gathered off the French Riviera. The first operations began during the night of August 14-15. French commandos neutralized the coastal batteries. Simultaneously, 5,000 American and British paratroopers were dropped behind the lines. At dawn, naval bombardments pummeled the shore. At 8 a.m., the first American assault waves landed on the beaches of Cavalaire, Saint-Tropez and Saint-Raphaël. The weak German defenses were quickly overwhelmed with the help of the local Resistance. On August 16, the French 1st Army of General de Lattre de Tassigny landed. Its first mission was to liberate Toulon and Marseille. After fierce street fighting, the German forces in Toulon capitulated on August 26, and Marseille fell on August 28. These two major ports became operational again within a few weeks, allowing the Allies to unload tons of supplies there. The Allied forces then advanced up the Rhône valley and joined with the troops coming from Normandy on September 12 near Dijon. This success accelerated the liberation of France and forced the German troops to withdraw toward the Vosges mountains and Alsace.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_provence_landing","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_provence_landing_title","SourceString":"PROVENCE LANDING","LocalizedString":"PROVENCE LANDING"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_provence_landing_text","SourceString":"Units you deploy this turn move into the frontline if possible.","LocalizedString":"Units you deploy this turn move into the frontline if possible."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_provence_landing_history","SourceString":"On August 15, 1944, the Allied forces launched Operation Dragoon, the landing in Provence. A fleet of nearly 2,000 ships gathered off the French Riviera. The first operations began during the night of August 14-15. French commandos neutralized the coastal batteries. Simultaneously, 5,000 American and British paratroopers were dropped behind the lines. At dawn, naval bombardments pummeled the shore. At 8 a.m., the first American assault waves landed on the beaches of Cavalaire, Saint-Tropez and Saint-Raphaël. The weak German defenses were quickly overwhelmed with the help of the local Resistance. On August 16, the French 1st Army of General de Lattre de Tassigny landed. Its first mission was to liberate Toulon and Marseille. After fierce street fighting, the German forces in Toulon capitulated on August 26, and Marseille fell on August 28. These two major ports became operational again within a few weeks, allowing the Allies to unload tons of supplies there. The Allied forces then advanced up the Rhône valley and joined with the troops coming from Normandy on September 12 near Dijon. This success accelerated the liberation of France and forced the German troops to withdraw toward the Vosges mountains and Alsace.","LocalizedString":"On August 15, 1944, the Allied forces launched Operation Dragoon, the landing in Provence. A fleet of nearly 2,000 ships gathered off the French Riviera. The first operations began during the night of August 14-15. French commandos neutralized the coastal batteries. Simultaneously, 5,000 American and British paratroopers were dropped behind the lines. At dawn, naval bombardments pummeled the shore. At 8 a.m., the first American assault waves landed on the beaches of Cavalaire, Saint-Tropez and Saint-Raphaël. The weak German defenses were quickly overwhelmed with the help of the local Resistance. On August 16, the French 1st Army of General de Lattre de Tassigny landed. Its first mission was to liberate Toulon and Marseille. After fierce street fighting, the German forces in Toulon capitulated on August 26, and Marseille fell on August 28. These two major ports became operational again within a few weeks, allowing the Allies to unload tons of supplies there. The Allied forces then advanced up the Rhône valley and joined with the troops coming from Normandy on September 12 near Dijon. This success accelerated the liberation of France and forced the German troops to withdraw toward the Vosges mountains and Alsace."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_4.0"},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/PROVENCE_LANDING.PROVENCE_LANDING","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_provence_landing_photo","SourceString":"Allied troops landing on Cavalaire beach, France, August 1944.","LocalizedString":"Allied troops landing on Cavalaire beach, France, August 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized","isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"inEffect","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_provence_landing","owner":"card_event_provence_landing_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_Ubergr